<title>CHINA: China August trade surplus $3.0 billion - customs.</title>
<headline>China August trade surplus $3.0 billion - customs.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's trade surplus was $3.0 billion in August, according to customs figures released by state television.</p>
<p>		     August 1996	  August 1995</p>
<p> Exports	    14.1		   12.53</p>
<p> Imports	    11.17		  11.59</p>
<p> Balance	   + 3.0		  + 0.94</p>
<p>(Note: the figures implied a rounding of the data)  </p>
<p>China had a trade surplus of $1.12 billion in July, customs figures showed.</p>
<p>The surplus for the first seven months was $2.01 billion, down from an extremely strong $14.3 billion in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Customs did not give a figure for the first eight months.</p>
</text>
